seed_audit.py: the soak tools' operand streams and the stress driver's seed schedule

== 1. THE PORT, held to the real tools' operands (tool_probe.out)
CHECK tool_probe.out holds the tools' operands: 3 operations x (3 seeds in B + 3 in C) streams ok (18 streams)
   evaluation order bands[rng() % 7] first : 18 of 18 streams match the tool (288 lanes)
   evaluation order (rng() % 3) first      : 1 of 18 streams match the tool (288 lanes)
CHECK one evaluation order reproduces every stream the tool printed, lane for lane           ok (18 of 18, 288 lanes)
   the compiled tool (gcc 11.4, this tree's host/Makefile flags) drew bands[rng() % 7] first
CHECK the other evaluation order does NOT match (the probe distinguishes the two orders)     ok (1 of 18)
CHECK CONTROL: a port with the third shift 16 instead of 17 does not match the tool          ok (0 of 18)
CHECK CONTROL: a port without `| 1` does not match every stream the tool printed             ok (9 of 18)
CHECK the port gives seeds 0x50AC0002 and 0x50AC0003 one stream, and 0x50AC0003 and 0x50AC0004 two ok 
CHECK CONTROL: without `| 1` the port gives those two seeds two streams                      ok 
CHECK two slices that share a state (counts 5,000 and 8,000): the shorter is the longer's prefix ok 

== 1b. DOES THE STREAM DEPEND ON THE COMPILER? (eval_order.out: the same source, built several ways)
CHECK eval_order.out holds seven builds of 9 streams each                                    ok (7 builds)
   build         bands-first (rng()%3)-first   neither
   gcc11-O0           8 of 9         0 of 9         0
   gcc11-O1           8 of 9         0 of 9         0
   gcc11-O2           8 of 9         0 of 9         0
   gcc11-O3           8 of 9         0 of 9         0
   gcc12-O0           8 of 9         0 of 9         0
   gcc12-O2           8 of 9         0 of 9         0
   gcc12-O3           8 of 9         0 of 9         0
CHECK every build's streams are reproduced by the port in ONE of the two orders (none unexplained) ok 
   orders seen across the 7 builds: bands
   -> every build here drew the same order; C still leaves it unspecified, so a build elsewhere may differ

== 2. THE SCHEDULE: how many (item, n) slices start from a state another slice started from
CHECK the driver's catalog has 54 random items                                               ok (54)
   54 random items x n = 0 .. 56 (the stress run reached n = 56)
   schedule                                               slices distinct shared states slices sharing
   as run: seed = base + 7919 n, then | 1                   3078     1597         1481           2962
   the same without the | 1 the tools apply                 3078     3078            0              0
   A: (item << 40) | (n << 1) | 1                           3078     3078            0              0
   B: mix64(key ^ (item << 32 | n)) | 1                     3078     3078            0              0
CHECK as run, 96% or more of the slices share a state with another item's slice              ok (2962 of 3078)
CHECK without the `| 1` the same seeds never collide (the collisions ARE the `| 1`)          ok 
CHECK schedule A has no shared state                                                         ok 
CHECK schedule B has no shared state                                                         ok 

seed_audit: every CHECK held
